  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2705.01 Revocation of Hospital Emergency Permit",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2705.01 Revocation of Hospital Emergency Permit.\n\n(a) The commissioner shall, after notice and opportunity for an administrative hearing, revoke a permittee's hospital emergency permit and demand its surrender upon showing that:\n\n(1) The permittee's driver license has been revoked or suspended;\n\n(2) The permittee is no longer designated by the hospital administrator as hospital emergency personnel and the permittee refuses to surrender the permit to the department;\n\n(3) The permittee utilized a vehicle displaying active emergency lights for a non-hospital emergency; or\n\n(4) The permittee violated any provision of these rules.\n\n(b) Permittees who have had their hospital emergency permit revoked shall immediately remove any emergency lights that are attached to their vehicle.\n\nSource. #4976, eff 11-14-90; ss and moved by #6174, eff\n\n1-26-96 (from Saf-C 2702), EXPIRED: 1-26-04\n\nNew. #8073, eff 4-23-04; ss by #10084, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13214-A, eff 6-16-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2700.html"
